                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Horizontal shoot 'em up with nice chiptune music. However, there's only one boring background, space, so no stage variety beyond enemy composition. Annoying full-screen effect when you destroy certain \"eyes\". Only around 10 types of enemies, but a choice of 25 characters, mostly cartoony skins of famous movie characters and superheroes. The bosses don't have enough attack types and take too long to kill, except for the first one. The game controls only with d-pad, not analog stick, on your gampead but well enough otherwise. Cool \"time distort\" slow-motion mechanic that you can use relatively often. I also appreciated the choice of two bonuses between stages. The game is not bad, but it's not good enough for a QD recommendation, especially at the regular price of $10.",
